1
00:05:03,333 --> 00:05:09,333
The story of a man who took the law into his own finger!

2
00:10:06,666 --> 00:10:12,666
Support Your Local Gunfighter is a comedy,
western film directed by Burt Kennedy.

3
00:15:10,000 --> 00:15:16,000
A con artist arrives in a mining town controlled by two competing companies.

4
00:20:13,333 --> 00:20:19,333
Both companies think he's a famous gunfighter and try to
hire him to drive the other out of town.

5
00:25:16,666 --> 00:25:22,666
Latigo, played by James Garner.

6
00:30:20,000 --> 00:30:26,000
Patience, played by Suzanne Pleshette.

7
00:35:23,333 --> 00:35:29,333
Jug May, played by Jack Elam.

8
00:40:26,666 --> 00:40:32,666
Taylor, played by Harry Morgan.

9
00:45:30,000 --> 00:45:36,000
Jenny, played by Joan Blondell.

10
00:50:33,333 --> 00:50:39,333
Goldie, played by Marie Windsor.

11
00:55:36,666 --> 00:55:42,666
Support Your Local Gunfighter is a 1971 American comic Western film directed by
Burt Kennedy and starring James Garner and Suzanne Pleshette.

12
01:00:40,000 --> 01:00:46,000
The screenplay was originally written by James Edward Grant, who died in
1966; Kennedy rewrote it but let Grant keep sole credit.

13
01:05:43,333 --> 01:05:49,333
The picture shares many cast and crew members and plot elements
with the earlier Support Your Local Sheriff!

14
01:10:46,666 --> 01:10:52,666
but is not a sequel.

15
01:15:50,000 --> 01:15:56,000
The supporting cast features Jack Elam, Harry Morgan, John Dehner,
Marie Windsor, Dub Taylor, Joan Blondell and Ellen Corby.

16
01:20:53,333 --> 01:20:59,333
Garner later wrote that the film was, "not as good
as Support Your Local Sheriff".

17
01:25:56,666 --> 01:26:02,666
The tone is lighthearted.
